#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151800 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152052 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93415651-fbcb-56d3-ad93-2b7f34e7bf4c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Negated Sentence in Symbolic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "f652a287-03b1-5e0b-9d77-9a681b1bb873" :question/math-academy-id "e-12681" :question/problem "Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\dfrac12$ is **not** a natural number, or $\\sqrt{2}$ is **not** a real number.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- ![](images/5a/5aa4f3afde005cff577fd75ebfa69e37861edf2628383b1191bf5c07b30fdde6.png)\n\n- ![](images/4c/4cbf587cfd90afaa031f87215c369495a23d50b886cda984b6a9a83a98ba7f06.png)" :question/worked-solution "The sentence\n\n $\\dfrac12$ is **not** a natural number \n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $\\neg P.$ \n\nThe sentence\n\n$\\sqrt{2}$ is **not** a real number \n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $\\neg Q.$\n\nTherefore, the sentence\n\n $\\dfrac12$ is **not** a natural number, or $\\sqrt{2}$ is **not** a real number\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $\\neg P \\lor \\neg Q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151801 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c49d316-3552-5ace-a749-5070b64230c3" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Truth Table for a Compound Statement"}] :question/id #uuid "3e19d03f-5298-52f4-a839-b4b7c5a1a4bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-12682" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\, \\neg (P \\land \\neg Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we add a column for $\\neg Q.$ Remember that the truth values of $\\neg Q$ are opposite those of $Q.$\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\, \\neg Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $P \\land \\neg Q.$ Remember that $P \\land \\neg Q$ is true if both $P$ and $\\neg Q$ are true.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\, \\neg Q\\,$ | $\\, P \\land \\neg Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nFinally, we add a column for $\\neg ( P \\land \\neg Q ).$ Remember that the truth values of $\\neg (P \\land \\neg Q)$ are opposite those of $P \\land \\neg Q.$\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\, \\neg Q\\,$ | $\\, P \\land \\neg Q\\,$ | $\\, \\neg (P \\land \\neg Q) \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151802 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69612c9a-699f-5635-8c9c-649a93ab4583" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Double Negation"}] :question/id #uuid "503739b1-ea2e-5c6a-8270-6e1fdc050bc4" :question/math-academy-id "e-12683" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $\\neg(\\neg C) \\lor \\neg(\\neg(C \\land D)).$" :question/worked-solution "Two negations in a row cancel each other out. So: \n\n- we can simplify $\\neg(\\neg C)$ to $C,$ and\n\n- we can also simplify $\\neg(\\neg(C \\land D))$ to $C \\land D.$\n\nTherefore, the given statement can be simplified to \n\n$$\nC \\lor (C \\land D).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151803 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "637030d2-d58f-56af-bf16-f33f755b65f9" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Plain English Statement"}] :question/id #uuid "e803903e-e272-5bd9-97a2-6b7cf12c359c" :question/math-academy-id "e-12702" :question/problem "Consider the following statement.\n\n$P: 1$ is **not** smaller than $2$\n\nWhat statement represents $\\neg P?$" :question/worked-solution "The symbol \"$\\neg$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\nIt is **not** true that $1$ is **not** smaller than $2.$\n\nIn other words, $1$ is smaller than $2.$ Therefore, $\\neg P$ means the following:\n\n$1$ is smaller than $2.$\n\nNote that $P$ is **false,** while $\\neg P$ is **true.**"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69612c9a-699f-5635-8c9c-649a93ab4583" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Double Negation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fcaeecd-cf3a-5c08-98ff-f6eee40e6c26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373731} {:answer/id #uuid "1031095e-8154-522f-aa31-a20ad0615f1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧¬B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373732} {:answer/id #uuid "90da550f-0bf8-5fd1-a6d6-8d976b712516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373733} {:answer/id #uuid "61b00b0d-0a9b-5f79-9404-6366bab23026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373734} {:answer/id #uuid "5589ef41-0669-5fb2-8146-7f86610b2488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fcaeecd-cf3a-5c08-98ff-f6eee40e6c26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373731} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a280d17-538b-56a2-aa41-636449a70fa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3eef300b-cac2-58c6-b154-4ab49b1b09c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-127790" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $¬(¬A)∨B.$" :question/worked-solution "Two negations in a row cancel each other out. So, we can simplify $¬(¬A)$ to $A.$\n\nTherefore, the given statement can be simplified to \n\n$$\nA∨B.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570769 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "637030d2-d58f-56af-bf16-f33f755b65f9" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Plain English Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68bfd57d-fa36-5445-b828-5494cf078835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ is prime." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570307} {:answer/id #uuid "9066a6d8-885f-5ac1-8ccb-7d1906cf46b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ is not prime." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570377} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d0fab5-8227-5fdf-bb2d-d19008bcda67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-5$ is not prime." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570452} {:answer/id #uuid "df66b2b7-6fa7-5d75-b69d-be975bbfdb6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-5$ is integer." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570517} {:answer/id #uuid "f6748b75-41f1-5324-a293-87ac93c5412d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-5$ is prime." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68bfd57d-fa36-5445-b828-5494cf078835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ is prime." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570307} :answer-field/id #uuid "7063af17-d8e4-57be-8ae9-215fbc4c689c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b52e0c2d-bb10-5ec6-8bde-b55f004808c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-176050" :question/problem "Consider the following statement.\n\n$5$ is **not** prime.\n\nWhat is the negation of this statement?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the given statement as $P.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\nIt is **not** true that $5$ is **not** prime.\n\nIn other words, $5$ is prime. Therefore, $¬P$ means the following:\n\n$5$ is prime.\n\nNote that $P$ is **false,** while $¬P$ is **true.**"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "637030d2-d58f-56af-bf16-f33f755b65f9" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Plain English Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2484b67d-ab16-5735-844a-ca86e906b916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "not $2$ divides $8.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570190} {:answer/id #uuid "580d1f85-8b99-5ed3-b9ee-03dc4529cefb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ divides $2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570280} {:answer/id #uuid "6d64e32e-84d5-541b-9f38-ffde8b5b23a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ does not divide $8.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570318} {:answer/id #uuid "ba4d40d3-08e3-5259-ac23-0789dc39447a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ divides $8.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570454} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a87c8b-acf2-51f1-b3e8-52aaedb33a77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ does not divide $2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d64e32e-84d5-541b-9f38-ffde8b5b23a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ does not divide $8.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570318} :answer-field/id #uuid "87729f27-60f8-5e17-816a-abea61b2c735" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d714d9e-2644-5dbb-a0ee-6c22b2b05b9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-176052" :question/problem "Given the statement\n\n$$\nP:2\\text{ divides }8\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following represents the statement $¬P?$" :question/worked-solution "The symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$$\n¬P:\\text{It is not true that }2\\text{ divides }8,\n$$\n\n \n\nIn other words, $2$ does *not* divide $8.$ Therefore, $¬P$ means the following:\n\n$$\n¬P:2\\text{ does }\\text{not}\\text{ divide }8.\n$$\n\nNote that $P$ is **true,** while $¬P$ is **false.**"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "637030d2-d58f-56af-bf16-f33f755b65f9" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Plain English Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0f83d2e-4fda-530c-bc0b-3fc197b6e9e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ belongs to the set of integer numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570408} {:answer/id #uuid "b062e970-b597-5f2d-9ea2-1cb272c3ae68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ does not belong to the set of integer numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570444} {:answer/id #uuid "b62f3fa3-82f7-5705-a6ab-076ed90d5359" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ belongs to the set of real numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570451} {:answer/id #uuid "c86f63a3-53c8-5588-8c96-c80888a795ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ belongs to the set of natural numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570473} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a64e58-305e-5436-b531-8fa978d44736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ does not belong to the set of real numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b062e970-b597-5f2d-9ea2-1cb272c3ae68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ does not belong to the set of integer numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570444} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c9f8a2e-fb8d-538e-8b0d-f6a1cc695c5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570648}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66c0453d-a98f-5149-84be-bb8778729997" :question/math-academy-id "q-176853" :question/problem "Consider the following statement.\n\n$5$ belongs to the set of integer numbers.\n\nWhat is the negation of this statement?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the given statement as $P.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\nIt is not true that $5$  belongs to the set of integer numbers.\n\nIn other words, $5$ does *not* belong to the set of integer numbers. Therefore, $¬P$ means the following:\n\n$5$ does **not** belong to the set of integer numbers.\n\nNote that $P$ is **true,** while $¬P$ is **false.**"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "637030d2-d58f-56af-bf16-f33f755b65f9" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Plain English Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05bf2d6f-5175-53ff-9053-2c1ced6b2262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.75$ belongs to the set of rational numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570133} {:answer/id #uuid "354af9d2-1125-500a-b5bd-0863a1344b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.75$ belongs to the set of real numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570218} {:answer/id #uuid "a356e9e1-1a39-5ac7-a858-418ad0ce302c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.75$ belongs to the set of integer numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570414} {:answer/id #uuid "d88400d3-4298-5734-96e2-da31e2bf5bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.75$ does not belong to the set of integer numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570503} {:answer/id #uuid "ee0939ad-c944-541e-8ce8-faa4bba0afcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.75$ does not belong to the set of rational numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05bf2d6f-5175-53ff-9053-2c1ced6b2262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.75$ belongs to the set of rational numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570133} :answer-field/id #uuid "522716aa-b013-56ac-9682-3c4f1235059c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32db5c7a-ebc7-5981-a2ce-a4afccfedb03" :question/math-academy-id "q-176857" :question/problem "Consider the following statement.\n\n$0.75$ does **not** belong to the set of rational numbers.\n\nWhat is the negation of this statement?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the given statement as $P.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\nIt is **not** true that $0.75$ does **not** belong to the set of rational numbers.\n\nIn other words, $0.75$ belongs to the set of rational numbers. Therefore, $¬P$ means the following:\n\n$0.75$ belongs to the set of rational numbers.\n\nNote that $P$ is **false,** while $¬P$ is **true.**"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "637030d2-d58f-56af-bf16-f33f755b65f9" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Plain English Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d826904-96a2-59ce-b5fc-60b5526a1ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$  is not greater than  $0.1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401669} {:answer/id #uuid "390a4ec3-5b8a-5b98-bc89-d674abef5a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.1$  is not greater than $0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401670} {:answer/id #uuid "b53fd129-b8e8-5685-a1f6-07230f89a1dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$  is equal to $0.1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401671} {:answer/id #uuid "252daeb4-b00c-5b00-87cc-5e54a6b731b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.1$  is greater than $0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401672} {:answer/id #uuid "778d6c76-109a-5c81-a30f-11950a9705cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$  is greater than  $0.1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "778d6c76-109a-5c81-a30f-11950a9705cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$  is greater than  $0.1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401673} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4cf313f-d1b6-5abf-b5ce-f86b65e36b0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0f8781c-d297-5aca-886f-46748c33ed7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-176859" :question/problem "Given the statement\n\n$$\nP:0\\text{ is }\\text{not}\\text{ greater than }0.1\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following represents $¬P?$" :question/worked-solution "The symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$$\n¬P:\\text{It is }\\text{not}\\text{ true that }0\\text{ is }\\text{not}\\text{ greater than }0.1,\n$$\n\n \n\nIn other words, $0$ is greater than $0.1.$ Therefore, $¬P$ means the following:\n\n$$\n¬P:0\\text{ is greater than }0.1.\n$$\n\nNote that $P$ is **true,** while $¬P$ is **false.**"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152052 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93415651-fbcb-56d3-ad93-2b7f34e7bf4c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Negated Sentence in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bbabc14-89b5-5b77-a784-cff4aed0e148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374382} {:answer/id #uuid "bfab0197-6d37-5fc4-a1c4-bbe99dfd09a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∨¬Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374383} {:answer/id #uuid "9356f5ec-c083-58b9-a82c-25a7d3120aeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧¬Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374384} {:answer/id #uuid "ebf2503a-db38-5662-8544-abfbe17df097" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374385} {:answer/id #uuid "28c9553f-250f-580f-ab0d-7b7b937a95da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bbabc14-89b5-5b77-a784-cff4aed0e148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374382} :answer-field/id #uuid "029abbce-a850-50fd-8647-5ad49e35afd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "729fc934-c5f0-55ad-a18c-489e8aabb842" :question/math-academy-id "q-176863" :question/problem "$10$ is **not** a prime number, and $0.1$ is a real number.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $P:10\\text{ is a prime number}$\n\n- $Q:0.1\\text{ is a real number}$" :question/worked-solution "The negation is represented by the symbol \"$¬$\".\n\nThe sentence\n\n$10$ is **not** a prime number \n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬P.$ \n\nThe sentence\n\n$0.1$ is a real number \n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the sentence\n\n$10$ is **not** a prime number, and $0.1$ is a real number\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬P∧Q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152052 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93415651-fbcb-56d3-ad93-2b7f34e7bf4c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Negated Sentence in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca03f4c6-f43c-599e-ae00-4805c10c1a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398633} {:answer/id #uuid "6c488ba2-23ee-5b95-ab2f-5cc4c289bd14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∨¬Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398634} {:answer/id #uuid "04dfe78b-c811-5b57-8684-5e4f44c6e6fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬(P∨Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398635} {:answer/id #uuid "253f3d0c-3686-58c6-b0b3-fee8f8709936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398636} {:answer/id #uuid "6f871f5a-c1eb-5f12-8176-b04fd5f551f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∧¬Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "253f3d0c-3686-58c6-b0b3-fee8f8709936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398636} :answer-field/id #uuid "4aa8db07-0769-5153-9ab7-dcb3cda6e4d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9b8bbb71-5c94-5fce-b0d2-f79d72a9b4c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-176865" :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{2}$ is **not** a rational number, or $-2$ is negative.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $P:\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ is a rational number}$\n\n- $Q:-2\\text{ is negative}$" :question/worked-solution "The sentence\n\n$\\frac{1}{2}$ is **not** a rational number \n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬P.$ \n\nThe sentence\n\n$-2$ is negative\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the sentence\n\n$\\frac{1}{2}$ is **not** a rational number, or $-2$ is negative\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬P∨Q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152052 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93415651-fbcb-56d3-ad93-2b7f34e7bf4c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Negated Sentence in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e091526-5ffd-5591-8887-aa1b671775f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∧¬Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570264} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab01873-1aba-5e67-8f54-84e85bbe60c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∨¬Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570343} {:answer/id #uuid "ad501c17-03fd-53ff-b60a-18b182a89e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨¬Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570432} {:answer/id #uuid "bd87453b-82a3-54e7-9a9b-2a8aa6569d24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570460} {:answer/id #uuid "feccd406-14d2-548c-ae56-655fb981b594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧¬Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad501c17-03fd-53ff-b60a-18b182a89e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨¬Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570432} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1054d29-077f-5163-ac93-fb66f447c9b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "846f1209-a84b-5c13-a0c8-7374d18fc658" :question/math-academy-id "q-176866" :question/problem "$9$ is divisible by $4$, or $8$ is **not** divisible by $3.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $P:9\\text{ is divisible by }4$\n\n- $Q:8\\text{ is divisible by }3$" :question/worked-solution "The sentence\n\n$9$ is divisible by $4$ \n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $P.$ \n\nThe sentence\n\n$8$ is **not** divisible by $3$\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬Q.$\n\nTherefore, the sentence\n\n$9$ is divisible by $4$, or $8$ is **not** divisible by $3$\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $P∨¬Q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69612c9a-699f-5635-8c9c-649a93ab4583" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Double Negation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1122f251-d67c-55a2-8e23-d6d95e0c558f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨¬(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570156} {:answer/id #uuid "118c6ce4-f01f-5145-8949-7ebe99fdc863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∨(¬P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570157} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4635c9-f9d0-51bd-b53c-847253ef09a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∨(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570437} {:answer/id #uuid "ec53a8a7-f295-556c-9a28-b5baa9cca522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(P∧¬Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570537} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a1b0d9-0cc8-5b3a-b649-f994a316954f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0a1b0d9-0cc8-5b3a-b649-f994a316954f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570548} :answer-field/id #uuid "05fa9516-97d5-54de-8ad6-321a63ebc418" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "91ef8c77-f388-589e-b268-cf2103e707d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-176871" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $¬(¬P)∨¬(¬(P∧Q)).$" :question/worked-solution "Two negations in a row cancel each other out. So: \n\n- we can simplify $¬(¬P)$ to $P,$ and\n\n- we can also simplify $¬(¬(P∧Q))$ to $P∧Q.$\n\nTherefore, the given statement can be simplified to \n\n$$\nP∨(P∧Q).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410109 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c49d316-3552-5ace-a749-5070b64230c3" :knowledge-po