ty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "594bcd16-11e5-554c-954b-51c8f4ae33f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-182392" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, we add a column for $A∧B.$ Remember that $A∧B$ is true if both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $¬(A∧B).$ Remember that the truth values of $¬(A∧B)$ are opposite those of $A∧B.$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69612c9a-699f-5635-8c9c-649a93ab4583" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Double Negation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63e6489e-ffd1-5779-a7ce-e64a31c6d086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570299} {:answer/id #uuid "84cb76a1-f260-5149-ace6-05d679bff267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570355} {:answer/id #uuid "8d7cbbdf-5616-5de2-b313-b7b0600f3848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬A∧¬B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570372} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e7e3d4-7924-574c-986a-faac6726ed40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧¬B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570506} {:answer/id #uuid "e83f1abb-ac36-5329-80d9-b49d69b028b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e83f1abb-ac36-5329-80d9-b49d69b028b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570530} :answer-field/id #uuid "e24bf6e9-63fc-5389-a07c-31a47adb1c69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "928cf87e-e0b7-5063-acab-2224d29c8984" :question/math-academy-id "q-81357" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $¬(¬A)∧¬(¬B).$" :question/worked-solution "Two negations in a row cancel each other out. So:\n\n- we can simplify $¬(¬A)$ to $A,$ and\n\n- we can also simplify  $¬(¬B)$ to $B.$\n\nTherefore, the given statement can be simplified to \n\n$$\nA∧B.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69612c9a-699f-5635-8c9c-649a93ab4583" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Double Negation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00092e11-dfc2-522f-b7e7-9f9a2f677aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧B)∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375448} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb0eafe-3c5e-5119-81d5-fd4d25a57bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(¬A∧¬B)∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 175